# Build-context excludes for every service image. NW-001/NW-002.
#
# IMPORTANT: every Dockerfile in this repo builds with the VEKTOR/ PARENT
# directory as its context (see services/DOCKERFILES.md), and Docker reads
# `.dockerignore` from the context root — i.e. from `VEKTOR/.dockerignore`,
# not from this file's location.
#
# VEKTOR/ is not a git repository, so a file placed there is tracked by
# nothing and exists only on whichever machine created it. That is exactly
# what had happened: a VEKTOR/.dockerignore existed locally, and CI
# (edge-arm64.yml) built with no ignore file at all, sweeping every
# node_modules and .git in both checkouts into the context.
#
# This tracked copy is the source of truth. Keep VEKTOR/.dockerignore
# identical to it:
#
#     cp vektor-backend/.dockerignore ../.dockerignore
#
# release-images.yml does the equivalent copy in CI.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/dist-tests
**/.turbo
**/.git
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.next
demo-screenshots

# vektor-proto's generated client is gitignored, so it exists on a
# developer machine and not on a clean checkout. Excluding it makes the
# build behave identically either way — every image runs `pnpm codegen:ts`
# itself. Without this line a local build silently succeeds using the
# host's copy while the same build in CI fails with TS2307, which is
# precisely the bug NW-001 found.
vektor-proto/src/generated
